// A view with a front and a back:  it shows one side at a time.
// A view that extends it says what each side looks like, in `<draw "front">` and `"back"`.

a "double sided view" is a view where:
	// Which way it faces
	- its "direction" is one of up, down
		- it "is face (direction)"
	// Sent each time it turns over;  side is the way it faces now
	- it sends "flipped" with side as a direction
	- to turn it face up:
		set its direction to up
	- to turn it face down:
		set its direction to down
	// Flips it:  face up becomes face down, and back.
	- to turn it over:
		if it is face up
			turn it face down
		otherwise
			turn it face up
		send flipped with side = its direction
	// The front when it's face up, the back when it's face down.
	- to draw it:
		if it is face up
			draw its front
		otherwise
			draw its back
